id=a52sxq_aod_brightness
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: automatic AOD brightness with wallpaper AOD
author=kusti420
description=Automatic AOD brightness with wallpaper AOD (LCD_CONFIG_AOD_FULLSCREEN=1) without modifying AODService, so Galaxy Store can keep updating Always On Display. AODService's fullscreen "platform brightness" mode maps lux to nits through config_autoBrightnessLevels_doze / config_autoBrightnessDisplayValuesNits_doze; framework-res has them empty (only the S26 Ultra product overlay fills them), which left AOD at the lowest 2 nit level in any light. target/a52sxq/overlay now provides them, stepped like the stock A52s AOD index (<=2 / <=50 / <=100 / >100 lux -> 2 / 10 / 30 / 60 nit HLPM).
